# The wired-sharing toggle is a one-click action in the network menu, so it
# must not stop for a password to open (or close) the DHCP-server hole ufw's
# after.rules otherwise swallows silently. The device is resolved inside the
# script from whatever is actually plugged in, never taken as an argument, so
# nothing wider than the two valid modes is ever granted.
%wheel ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/omarchy-network-shared shared, /usr/bin/omarchy-network-shared wan
